<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka eases on higher dollar demand.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka eases on higher dollar demand.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka lost early gains and closed slightly easier at 42.5485/5500 to the dollar in interbank trading against the previous 42.5480/5500, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers said the local unit opened firmer at 42.5460/5500 but slipped on higher demand for the U.S. currency from importers.</p>
<p>The interbank call money rates ended unchanged at 4.0 to 4.75 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom 880-2-506363</p>
</text>
